-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_splices_err_escape.pcpp - Lexical: an escape that takes a spliced quote

  Break step of lex_splices: splices go before escapes, so of the two
  backslashes ending the string's first line the second is the splice and
  the first escapes the quote on the next line: the string never closes,
  LX0001, where it starts. The marked line ends in the splice, so its
  marker is a block-comment marker.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_splices_err_escape;

/*
  @@test
    kind error
  @@end
*/

begin
  println(/* // ERROR LX0001@39 // */ "a\\
");
end.
